comments.body:
@Navid200 I nearly never restart the sensor (logically I mean) and also never checked in Nightscout as the actual SAGE I was convinced was picked from the real sensor lifetime...
The rest of the discussion is indeed vocabulary accuracy and historical reasons. You can insert a Libre sensor and start it, at this point the logic is sane. But you can insert a sensor and not start it immediately. So I'd agree that the question should be "What time was it started?" since starting a Libre means you need to wait for an hour before you can get consistent readings (and you can get inconsistent readings during warmup if you like crazy numbers).
I would remove the dialog and rely on sensor information from FRAM. Start sensor should only be a way to say there's a new sensor, no time necessary as long as the information can be grabbed from the sensor FRAM (but don't rely on me to remember if this is always feasible, but I'd guess yes).
